00"} "Doubles, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "44000"} "1896"] "\n" [:option {:value "44028"} "1900"] "\n" [:option {:value "44077"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "926092"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "926128"} "1904"] "\n" [:option {:value "44210"} "1908"] "\n" [:option {:value "44337"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "44578"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "44715"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "900151"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "900254"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "900391"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "45037"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "45230"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "45440"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "45658"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "45876"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261879"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "324071"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "353205"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19004600"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2006500"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/607"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Singles, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "23 – 26 April 1906"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Intercalated"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/191"} "Homilos Antisfairiseos Athinon, Athina"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/44135"} "18 from 6 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12"} "Max Decugis"] " was relatively unchallenged in winning this title, losing only two games in eight sets and four matches prior to the final.  In the final, he defeated France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/19"} "Maurice Germot"] " in four sets (3-1).  Germot was probably favored, as he had been French singles champion in 1905-06, while Decugis had won that title in 1903-04."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Decugis was the greatest French tennis player prior to the “Four Musketeers” of the 1920’s.  He also has the greatest record of any Olympic tennis player, as he eventually won four Olympic gold medals and six Olympic medals in all:  Gold - 1906 singles, " [:a {:href "/results/44167"} "doubles"] ", and " [:a {:href "/results/44200"} "mixed"] "; and the " [:a {:href "/results/44692"} "1920 mixed"] " (with " [:a {:href "/athletes/2455"} "Suzanne Lenglen"] "); Silver - " [:a {:href "/results/44047"} "1900 doubles"] "; and Bronze - " [:a {:href "/results/44626"} "1920 doubles"] ".  In the French Championships, which were closed until 1925, Decugis won 33 titles between 1902 and 1920 - 8 singles, 14 doubles, 11 mixed.  His best performance at Wimbledon came in 1911 and 1912, when he made the singles’ semi-finals.  In 1911, he and " [:a {:href "/athletes/20"} "André Gobert"] " (FRA) won the gentlemen’s doubles, the first Frenchmen to win a Wimbledon title.  Decugis was also German singles champion in 1901-02."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Of note, " [:a {:href "/athletes/80023"} "“Guus” Kessler"] " (NED) made it through to the semi-finals without playing a match, being given the benefit of three walk-overs.  In the semis, he lost to Decugis love-love, thus finishing =4th in the Olympics without winning a single game."] "\n\n" [:p {} "None of the world’s top men’s players were in Athens in 1906.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/88"} "Laurie Doherty"] " (GBR) had been Wimbledon singles champion in 1902-06, and was probably the greatest player in the world.  Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/97"} "Arthur Wentworth Gore"] " was Wimbledon runner-up in 1906-07, and would win that title in 1908-09.  " [:a {:href "/athletes/1805033"} "Norman Brookes"] " of Australia was runner-up to Doherty in 1905, and would win the Wimbledon singles in 1907.  America’s top players were " [:a {:href "/athletes/2804"} "Beals Wright"] ", the defending Olympic champion from " [:a {:href "/results/44077"} "1904"] ", who won the 1905 United States’ singles title; and Bill Larned, U.S. singles champion in 1901-02 and 1907-11."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12"} "Max Decugis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/19"} "Maurice Germot"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/79850"} "Zdeněk Žemla"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BOH"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BOH.png"}] "BOH"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/80023"} "Guus Kessler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/80024"} "Gerard Scheurleer"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style